{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365115-tall-as-tall-can-be-paul-bunyan-and-spriggans","id":1365115,"title":"Tall as Tall can be (Paul Bunyan and Spriggans)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-03T14:35:22-08:00","id":1365115,"title":"Tall as Tall can be (Paul Bunyan and Spriggans)","content":"There are a number of ridiculous details about <i>Fate/Grand Order's</i> interpretation of Paul Bunyan that we don't need to get into here. I'd like to focus on her size. (Yes, &quot;her&quot;. It's <i>Fate</i>.)<br /> <br /> Drawing from her legend, Paul Bunyan is a giant of vague and indeterminate size. Out under the open sky, she can stand tall enough for her head to reach the clouds, and she can crush a whole moose underfoot with a single stomp. But she can freely enter any space with an effective ceiling, automatically and involuntarily shrinking to accommodate, though (if I read things right) she always remains too big to stand up straight until she's forced to assume the normal height for a little girl of her apparent age. Her shrinking and growing is so surreal that even when you're watching her do it, it's like your mind playing tricks on you.<br /> <br /> In <i>Exalted</i> mechanic terms, she enjoys the benefits of Legendary Size as long as she has enough vertical space to be a giant, but she can be denied those benefits by being confined.<br /> <br /> This seems like an excellent power for raksha to learn, and for inherent abilities for some species of Wyld Creatures (perhaps called Spriggans) and spirits.<br /> <br /> For demons, does this seem within the range of Second Circle Demons, or only for Third Circles?<br /> <br /> What level of elementals or gods might behave like this?<br /> <br /> Would you try to achieve this kind of situation power through sorcery or artifice? If so, how?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T19:17:57-08:00","id":1365158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365115-tall-as-tall-can-be-paul-bunyan-and-spriggans#post1365115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems like an excellent power for raksha to learn, and for inherent abilities for some species of Wyld Creatures (perhaps called Spriggans) and spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree (with slight variation depending on how their Charms are ultimately written).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For demons, does this seem within the range of Second Circle Demons, or only for Third Circles?</div> </div> </div> </div>Within my interpretation, it feels a bit closer to the Third Circle &quot;iconic force&quot; level than Second Circle &quot;heroic actor of Hell&quot;, although I can still imagine some arguments for the latter. I'd say it depends on what larger story is given for the demon in question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What level of elementals or gods might behave like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>That precognitive earth elemental is Essence 4, isn't he? I feel as though this might be the kind of power you'd give an elemental who falls within the category of &quot;entirely unique phenomenon&quot;, in which case it's not really dependent on Essence level (although perhaps not lower than 4). Really, you're kind of in the same space as the utterly gigantic volcanic behemoth, another being that is &quot;only&quot; Essence 5.<br /> <br /> For a god I feel as though the scope and grandeur of it is fitting only for 8 or 9.<br /> <br /> To me, either case is basically picturing somebody occupying a similar narrative to Mononoke's Night Walker striding over the landscape, and thinking about what types of the respective spirits live there. For gods that denotes great rank and therefor high Essence, for elementals it's more the other thing I said.<br /> <br /> Although even then... I could imagine a narrative for a god in question in which they function as a kind of sentinel figure, looming but subordinate, in which case it ends up as similar to the elementals in Essence level. I'd assume that such a god doesn't have much else that is formidable besides their great stature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you try to achieve this kind of situation power through sorcery or artifice? If so, how?</div> </div> </div> </div>The oddity of it feels more in line with sorcery to me. Some powerful working the sorcerer did that kind of uplifts and makes uncanny their being and presence. It's again kind of like the Night Walker, I'm picturing some weirdo who spends a lot of time filling up their home like the Ghost of Christmas Present and occasionally goes wandering around like the BFG to peek in on people's houses and do stuff with their dreams.<br /> <br /> Although... it actually does strike me as rather fitting for some powerful suit of armour, now that I think about it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}